            "level": {
                "value": 17
            },
            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>As ferocious in temperament as they are bizarre in appearance, thrasfyrs resemble six-limbed bears with bull-like horns, draconic scales, and a fire-breathing serpent for a tail. Every thrasfyr is wrapped in animated chains, reflections of its fundamental nature as a bound creature that it uses to likewise bind its foes. Like all the Tane, thrasfyrs were created as living weapons by the Eldest. With the ancient wars they were born to fight long ended, most thrasfyrs slumber in rugged, uninhabited regions.</p>\n<p>Though they are engineered beings, thrasfyrs are still living beasts that need to eat, drink, and sleep; they do age, as well, though they live such long lives that a thrasfyr succumbing to old age is vanishingly rare.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Pathfinder Feybound"
            }
